IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wcr-dates`

-- Workers Compensation Regulation 2016 (NSW) -- Part 2 (work-related diseases) with Schedules 1 and 2, as they meet a
-- worker who says a disease came from work.
--
-- SEAT. The injured worker. The Regulation's Part 2 only prescribes things for sections 19, 19A and 19B of the Workers
-- Compensation Act 1987 (presumptions that a disease is work-related); each question says which presumption it feeds.
-- The words of those sections are quoted from the deposited 1987 Act (subjects/au/nsw/workers-compensation-act-1987/
-- registers/source-bundle/act-1987-070.txt); the stable l4 cannot IMPORT across subjects.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no question answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE where the text's own words say no ("means", "if", a closed
-- list the Regulation prescribes), or NOTHING where the text does not answer on the facts given; each NOTHING carries a
-- "NOTHING-kind" comment. A presumption holds "unless the contrary is established": a JUST TRUE says the presumption is
-- available, not that the claim succeeds.
--
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website (as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Part 2 -- Work-related diseases`

§§ `cl 4 and Schedule 1 -- diseases taken to be work-related (1987 Act s 19(1))`

-- Schedule 1, Column 1. Brucellosis, leptospirosis and Q fever share one row; they are listed separately here because
-- clause 5 treats them separately.
DECLARE `Scheduled disease` IS ONE OF
    `poisoning by lead, its alloys or compounds`
    `poisoning by mercury, its amalgams or compounds`
    `anthrax infection`
    `phosphorus poisoning`
    `arsenic poisoning`
    `poisoning by benzene or its homologues or their nitro- and amido-derivatives`
    `poisoning by halogen derivatives of aliphatic hydrocarbons`
    `pathological manifestations due to radium, radioactive substances or X-rays`
    `primary epitheliomatous cancer of the skin`
    `brucellosis`
    `leptospirosis`
    `Q fever`
    `a disease not in Schedule 1`

-- Schedule 1, Column 2, in the order printed.
DECLARE `Scheduled employment` IS ONE OF
    `handling of ore containing lead, including fine shot in zinc factories`
    `casting of old zinc and lead in ingots`
    `manufacture of articles made of cast lead or lead alloys`
    `employment in the polygraphic industries`
    `manufacture of lead compounds`
    `manufacture and repair of electric accumulators`
    `preparation and use of enamels containing lead`
    `polishing by means of lead files or putty powder with a lead content`
    `painting operations with coating, cement or colouring substances containing lead pigments`
    `handling of mercury ore`
    `manufacture of mercury compounds`
    `manufacture of measuring and laboratory apparatus`
    `preparation of raw material for the hat-making industry`
    `hot gilding`
    `use of mercury pumps in the manufacture of incandescent lamps`
    `manufacture of fulminate of mercury primers`
    `work in connection with animals infected with anthrax`
    `handling of animal carcases or parts of them, including hides, hoofs and horns`
    `loading, unloading or transport of merchandise that has touched anthrax-infected animals or carcases`
    `a process producing, liberating or using phosphorus or its compounds`
    `a process producing, liberating or using arsenic or its compounds`
    `a process producing, liberating or using benzene or its homologues or their nitro- and amido-derivatives`
    `a process producing, liberating or using halogen derivatives of aliphatic hydrocarbons`
    `a process involving exposure to radium, radioactive substances or X-rays`
    `a process handling or using tar, pitch, bitumen, mineral oil, paraffin or their compounds, products or residues`
    `slaughtering of cattle on the slaughter-floor of an abattoir or slaughter-house`
    `handling or processing slaughtered cattle carcases in an abattoir or slaughter-house`
    `penning up or running cattle through a race at an abattoir or slaughter-house`
    `an activity incidental or necessary to those abattoir activities, on the slaughter-floor, where raw by-products are handled, or about a pen or race`
    `employment not in Schedule 1`

-- The rows of Schedule 1, one per disease entry in Column 1.
DECLARE `Schedule 1 row` IS ONE OF
    `the lead row`, `the mercury row`, `the anthrax row`, `the phosphorus row`, `the arsenic row`, `the benzene row`,
    `the halogen row`, `the radiation row`, `the skin cancer row`, `the cattle infections row`, `no row`

GIVEN `the disease` IS A `Scheduled disease`
GIVETH A `Schedule 1 row`
`the row of disease` `the disease` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the disease`
    WHEN `poisoning by lead, its alloys or compounds` THEN `the lead row`
    WHEN `poisoning by mercury, its amalgams or compounds` THEN `the mercury row`
    WHEN `anthrax infection` THEN `the anthrax row`
    WHEN `phosphorus poisoning` THEN `the phosphorus row`
    WHEN `arsenic poisoning` THEN `the arsenic row`
    WHEN `poisoning by benzene or its homologues or their nitro- and amido-derivatives` THEN `the benzene row`
    WHEN `poisoning by halogen derivatives of aliphatic hydrocarbons` THEN `the halogen row`
    WHEN `pathological manifestations due to radium, radioactive substances or X-rays` THEN `the radiation row`
    WHEN `primary epitheliomatous cancer of the skin` THEN `the skin cancer row`
    WHEN `brucellosis` THEN `the cattle infections row`
    WHEN `leptospirosis` THEN `the cattle infections row`
    WHEN `Q fever` THEN `the cattle infections row`
    OTHERWISE `no row`

GIVEN `the employment` IS A `Scheduled employment`
GIVETH A `Schedule 1 row`
`the row of employment` `the employment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the employment`
    WHEN `handling of ore containing lead, including fine shot in zinc factories` THEN `the lead row`
    WHEN `casting of old zinc and lead in ingots` THEN `the lead row`
    WHEN `manufacture of articles made of cast lead or lead alloys` THEN `the lead row`
    WHEN `employment in the polygraphic industries` THEN `the lead row`
    WHEN `manufacture of lead compounds` THEN `the lead row`
    WHEN `manufacture and repair of electric accumulators` THEN `the lead row`
    WHEN `preparation and use of enamels containing lead` THEN `the lead row`
    WHEN `polishing by means of lead files or putty powder with a lead content` THEN `the lead row`
    WHEN `painting operations with coating, cement or colouring substances containing lead pigments` THEN `the lead row`
    WHEN `handling of mercury ore` THEN `the mercury row`
    WHEN `manufacture of mercury compounds` THEN `the mercury row`
    WHEN `manufacture of measuring and laboratory apparatus` THEN `the mercury row`
    WHEN `preparation of raw material for the hat-making industry` THEN `the mercury row`
    WHEN `hot gilding` THEN `the mercury row`
    WHEN `use of mercury pumps in the manufacture of incandescent lamps` THEN `the mercury row`
    WHEN `manufacture of fulminate of mercury primers` THEN `the mercury row`
    WHEN `work in connection with animals infected with anthrax` THEN `the anthrax row`
    WHEN `handling of animal carcases or parts of them, including hides, hoofs and horns` THEN `the anthrax row`
    WHEN `loading, unloading or transport of merchandise that has touched anthrax-infected animals or carcases` THEN `the anthrax row`
    WHEN `a process producing, liberating or using phosphorus or its compounds` THEN `the phosphorus row`
    WHEN `a process producing, liberating or using arsenic or its compounds` THEN `the arsenic row`
    WHEN `a process producing, liberating or using benzene or its homologues or their nitro- and amido-derivatives` THEN `the benzene row`
    WHEN `a process producing, liberating or using halogen derivatives of aliphatic hydrocarbons` THEN `the halogen row`
    WHEN `a process involving exposure to radium, radioactive substances or X-rays` THEN `the radiation row`
    WHEN `a process handling or using tar, pitch, bitumen, mineral oil, paraffin or their compounds, products or residues` THEN `the skin cancer row`
    WHEN `slaughtering of cattle on the slaughter-floor of an abattoir or slaughter-house` THEN `the cattle infections row`
    WHEN `handling or processing slaughtered cattle carcases in an abattoir or slaughter-house` THEN `the cattle infections row`
    WHEN `penning up or running cattle through a race at an abattoir or slaughter-house` THEN `the cattle infections row`
    WHEN `an activity incidental or necessary to those abattoir activities, on the slaughter-floor, where raw by-products are handled, or about a pen or race` THEN `the cattle infections row`
    OTHERWISE `no row`

GIVEN `the row` IS A `Schedule 1 row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the row` `is a real row` IF
    CONSIDER `the row`
    WHEN `no row` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- cl 4(2) "A disease set out in Column 1 of Schedule 1 is prescribed as a disease that is related to the employment ...
-- set out in Column 2 of that Schedule opposite the description of that disease." 1987 Act s 19(1): "If a worker, during
-- a time when the worker is engaged in employment of a kind prescribed ..., contracts a disease prescribed ... as a
-- disease that is related to employment of that kind, then ..., unless the contrary is established -- (a) the disease
-- shall be deemed to have been contracted ... in the course of the employment ..., and (b) that employment shall be
-- deemed to have been a substantial contributing factor to the disease."
-- A pair not opposite each other in Schedule 1 answers JUST FALSE (fork F2): clause 4 prescribes only what the
-- Schedule sets out. The disease may still be shown to be work-related without the presumption.
@export Does Schedule 1 make my disease presumed to have come from my work (Regulation cl 4 and Schedule 1; 1987 Act s 19(1))? A yes means it is presumed unless the contrary is established.
GIVEN `my disease` IS A `Scheduled disease` @desc Your disease, chosen from the diseases in Column 1 of Schedule 1, or "a disease not in Schedule 1"
      `my employment` IS A `Scheduled employment` @desc The kind of work you were doing, chosen from Column 2 of Schedule 1, or "employment not in Schedule 1"
      `I contracted it while engaged in that employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you contracted the disease during a time when you were engaged in that kind of employment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does Schedule 1 presume my disease is work-related` MEANS
    IF     (`the row of disease` `my disease`) `is a real row`
       AND ((`the row of disease` `my disease`) EQUALS (`the row of employment` `my employment`))
    THEN IF `I contracted it while engaged in that employment`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `cl 5 and Schedule 2 Part 1 -- tests for brucellosis, Q fever and leptospirosis (1987 Act s 19(2))`

DECLARE `Cattle infection` IS ONE OF `brucellosis infection`, `Q fever infection`, `leptospirosis infection`

-- Schedule 2 Part 1, Column 2 (the tests), in the order printed.
DECLARE `Infection test` IS ONE OF
    `Brucella agglutination or complement fixation titres on paired acute and convalescent sera`
    `a single high Brucella agglutination titre or complement fixation test`
    `a laboratory culture for Brucella`
    `nucleic acid testing for Q fever`
    `Q fever phase II antigen on paired sera tested in parallel`
    `a laboratory culture for Q fever`
    `Q fever IgM`
    `Leptospira agglutination titres on paired acute and convalescent sera`
    `a single Leptospira micro agglutination titre supported by an EIA IgM result`
    `a laboratory culture for Leptospira`
    `another test`

DECLARE `Infection test facts` HAS
    `days between the two samples` IS A NUMBER
    `fold increase in antibody titre` IS A NUMBER
    `seroconversion shown` IS A BOOLEAN
    `single titre` IS A NUMBER
    `organism detected or isolated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `recent Q fever vaccination` IS A BOOLEAN
    `clinically compatible illness` IS A BOOLEAN
    `positive EIA IgM` IS A BOOLEAN

-- "taken at least 2 weeks apart": 14 days or more between the samples.
GIVEN `the facts` IS AN `Infection test facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the samples are at least 2 weeks apart` `the facts` IF `the facts`'s `days between the two samples` AT LEAST 14

GIVEN `the facts` IS AN `Infection test facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a four-fold or greater increase` `the facts` IF `the facts`'s `fold increase in antibody titre` AT LEAST 4

-- Each line: the disease the test belongs to, the test's own requirements (Column 2) and the result (Column 3).
GIVEN `the disease` IS A `Cattle infection`, `the test` IS AN `Infection test`, `the facts` IS AN `Infection test facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the test gives a prescribed result for` `the disease` `the test` `the facts` IF
    CONSIDER `the disease`
    WHEN `brucellosis infection` THEN
        CONSIDER `the test`
        WHEN `Brucella agglutination or complement fixation titres on paired acute and convalescent sera` THEN
                `the samples are at least 2 weeks apart` `the facts`
            AND (`the facts`'s `seroconversion shown` OR `there is a four-fold or greater increase` `the facts`)
        WHEN `a single high Brucella agglutination titre or complement fixation test` THEN `the facts`'s `single titre` AT LEAST 640
        WHEN `a laboratory culture for Brucella` THEN `the facts`'s `organism detected or isolated`
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `Q fever infection` THEN
        CONSIDER `the test`
        WHEN `nucleic acid testing for Q fever` THEN `the facts`'s `organism detected or isolated`
        WHEN `Q fever phase II antigen on paired sera tested in parallel` THEN
                `the samples are at least 2 weeks apart` `the facts`
            AND (NOT (`the facts`'s `recent Q fever vaccination`))
            AND (`the facts`'s `seroconversion shown` OR `there is a four-fold or greater increase` `the facts`)
        WHEN `a laboratory culture for Q fever` THEN `the facts`'s `organism detected or isolated`
        WHEN `Q fever IgM` THEN
                (NOT (`the facts`'s `recent Q fever vaccination`))
            AND `the facts`'s `clinically compatible illness`
            AND `the facts`'s `organism detected or isolated`
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `leptospirosis infection` THEN
        CONSIDER `the test`
        WHEN `Leptospira agglutination titres on paired acute and convalescent sera` THEN
                `the samples are at least 2 weeks apart` `the facts`
            AND `there is a four-fold or greater increase` `the facts`
        WHEN `a single Leptospira micro agglutination titre supported by an EIA IgM result` THEN
                `the facts`'s `positive EIA IgM`
            AND `the facts`'s `single titre` AT LEAST 400
        WHEN `a laboratory culture for Leptospira` THEN `the facts`'s `organism detected or isolated`
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- 1987 Act s 19(2): the disease "shall be deemed to have been contracted by a worker if the result of any medical test
-- (a) which complies with such requirements as are prescribed ... and (b) which was carried out for the purpose of
-- determining whether that worker has contracted that disease, is a result prescribed ...". cl 5 and Schedule 2 Part 1
-- prescribe the tests and results. "where possible, conducted at the same laboratory" (fork F3) is read as advice, not a
-- requirement.
@export Does my test result mean I am taken to have contracted brucellosis, Q fever or leptospirosis (Regulation cl 5 and Schedule 2 Part 1; 1987 Act s 19(2))?
GIVEN `the disease` IS A `Cattle infection` @desc Which of the three diseases the test was for
      `the test` IS AN `Infection test` @desc The medical test you had, chosen from Column 2 of Schedule 2 Part 1, or "another test"
      `the test was to find out whether I had the disease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the test was carried out to find out whether you had contracted that disease
      `days between the two samples` IS A NUMBER @desc For a paired test, the number of days between the two blood samples (0 if a single sample)
      `fold increase in antibody titre` IS A NUMBER @desc For a paired test, how many times higher the antibody titre was in the second sample (for example 4 for a four-fold rise; 0 if none)
      `seroconversion shown` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a paired test, whether the result showed seroconversion (IgG seroconversion for brucellosis)
      `single titre` IS A NUMBER @desc For a single titre test, the antibody titre reported (for example 640 for 1:640; 0 if none)
      `organism detected or isolated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a culture, nucleic acid or IgM test, whether the organism (or IgM) was detected or isolated
      `recent Q fever vaccination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had been recently vaccinated against Q fever before the test
      `clinically compatible illness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the Q fever IgM test, whether you had a compatible illness: fever, sweating and chills, severe headache, muscle and joint pain, extreme fatigue, weakness and malaise
      `positive EIA IgM` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the single Leptospira titre, whether a positive EIA IgM result supported it
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does my test show I contracted the disease` MEANS
    IF     `the test was to find out whether I had the disease`
       AND `the test gives a prescribed result for` `the disease` `the test` (`Infection test facts` WITH
                `days between the two samples` IS `days between the two samples`
                `fold increase in antibody titre` IS `fold increase in antibody titre`
                `seroconversion shown` IS `seroconversion shown`
                `single titre` IS `single titre`
                `organism detected or isolated` IS `organism detected or isolated`
                `recent Q fever vaccination` IS `recent Q fever vaccination`
                `clinically compatible illness` IS `clinically compatible illness`
                `positive EIA IgM` IS `positive EIA IgM`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `cl 5A -- firefighting bodies (1987 Act s 19A)`

DECLARE `Firefighting body` IS ONE OF
    `the NSW Rural Fire Service`
    `Fire and Rescue NSW`
    `the Office of Environment and Heritage`
    `the Forestry Corporation`
    `Sydney Trains`
    `another body or agency`

-- cl 5A prescribes the five bodies for s 19A. s 19A(3): "A worker has been engaged in firefighting employment if -- (a)
-- the worker has, at any time, been employed by any person, body or agency (or former body or agency) prescribed ...,
-- and (b) in the course of that employment, the worker has performed firefighting activities." The other limbs of s 19A
-- (the Schedule 4 cancers and their qualifying service periods) are in the 1987 Act and not encoded here.
@export Have I been engaged in firefighting employment, for the firefighters' cancer presumption (Regulation cl 5A; 1987 Act s 19A(3))?
GIVEN `my employer` IS A `Firefighting body` @desc The body or agency you were employed by, chosen from those clause 5A prescribes, or "another body or agency"
      `I performed firefighting activities in that employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in that employment, you extinguished, controlled or prevented the spread of fire, did bush fire hazard reduction work, or trained others in those activities with exposure to smoke or fire hazards
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Have I been engaged in firefighting employment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my employer`
    WHEN `another body or agency` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE IF `I performed firefighting activities in that employment`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `cll 5B-5D -- COVID-19 (1987 Act s 19B)`

-- 1987 Act s 19B(9) "prescribed employment means employment in any of the following -- (a) ... (n)", and "(o) any other
-- type of employment prescribed by the regulations", which cl 5D does: (a) cafes, (b) supermarkets, (c) funeral homes,
-- (d) child care facilities.
DECLARE `Kind of workplace` IS ONE OF
    `the retail industry (not only on-line retail)`
    `a business providing only on-line retail`
    `the health care sector, including ambulance officers and public health employees`
    `disability and aged care facilities`
    `educational institutions (not only on-line teaching)`
    `an establishment providing only on-line teaching`
    `police and emergency services, including fire brigades and rural fire services`
    `refuges, halfway houses and homeless shelters`
    `passenger transport services`
    `libraries`
    `courts and tribunals`
    `correctional centres and detention centres`
    `restaurants, clubs and hotels`
    `the construction industry`
    `places of public entertainment or instruction`
    `the cleaning industry`
    `cafes`
    `supermarkets`
    `funeral homes`
    `child care facilities`
    `another kind of employment`

-- s 19B(6) "This section applies to a casual worker in prescribed employment only if the worker has performed casual
-- work in the employment on 1 or more of the 21 days preceding the date of the injury."
@export Is my work "prescribed employment" for the COVID-19 presumption (1987 Act s 19B(9), (6); Regulation cl 5D)?
GIVEN `my workplace` IS A `Kind of workplace` @desc The kind of employment you were in, chosen from the list in s 19B(9) and clause 5D, or "another kind of employment"
      `I am a casual worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a casual worker in that employment
      `I did casual work there in the 21 days before the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If casual, whether you performed casual work in that employment on at least one of the 21 days before the date of the injury
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my work prescribed employment for COVID-19` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my workplace`
    WHEN `a business providing only on-line retail` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an establishment providing only on-line teaching` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `another kind of employment` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE IF `I am a casual worker` AND (NOT `I did casual work there in the 21 days before the injury`)
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `COVID-19 test` IS ONE OF
    `a SARS-CoV-2 nucleic acid test listed in the Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods`
    `a laboratory culture confirmed with a PCR test listed in the Australian Register of Therapeutic Goods`
    `another COVID-19 test`

-- cl 5B(1) and Schedule 2 Part 2: the nucleic acid test, result "Detection of SARS-CoV-2"; the culture with PCR
-- confirmation, result "The isolation of SARS-CoV-2, confirmed with PCR". 1987 Act s 19B(2): the worker "is taken to
-- have contracted COVID-19" if the result of a prescribed test, carried out to find out, is a prescribed result.
-- cl 5B(2) makes the s 19B(3) clinical criteria the same results, so a classification adds no other route.
@export Does my test mean I am taken to have contracted COVID-19 (Regulation cl 5B and Schedule 2 Part 2; 1987 Act s 19B(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the test` IS A `COVID-19 test` @desc The test you had: an ARTG-listed SARS-CoV-2 nucleic acid (PCR) test, a laboratory culture confirmed with an ARTG-listed PCR test, or another test (for example a rapid antigen test)
      `the test was to find out whether I had COVID-19` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the test was carried out to find out whether you had COVID-19
      `SARS-CoV-2 was detected or isolated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the test detected SARS-CoV-2 (or, for a culture, isolated it and PCR confirmed it)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does my test show I contracted COVID-19` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the test`
    WHEN `another COVID-19 test` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE IF `the test was to find out whether I had COVID-19` AND `SARS-CoV-2 was detected or isolated`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE

-- cl 5C(1) "For the purposes of section 19B(5)(a) ..., the relevant date is the later of -- (a) the date that is 21 days
-- after the date of the injury, or (b) if a medical practitioner issues a certificate of capacity certifying that the
-- worker still has COVID-19 on that date -- the date that marks the end of the expected duration of the worker's
-- incapacity for work as a result of COVID-19 that is specified in the certificate." s 19B(5): presumed incapable of work
-- "for the period starting on the date of the injury and ending (unless sooner ended by the death of the worker) -- (a)
-- on a date established in accordance with the regulations". s 19B(4): the date of injury is the first of diagnosis,
-- classification or death.
@export Until what date am I presumed unable to work because of COVID-19 (Regulation cl 5C(1); 1987 Act s 19B(5))?
GIVEN `the date of my injury` IS A DATE @desc The date of injury for COVID-19: the day a doctor first diagnosed or classified you as having COVID-19
      `a certificate says I still have COVID-19 on day 21` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a doctor issued a certificate of capacity certifying that you still had COVID-19 on the day 21 days after the date of injury
      `the end of the incapacity the certificate expects` IS A DATE @desc The date the certificate gives as the end of the expected duration of your incapacity (any date if there is no such certificate)
GIVETH A DATE
`Until when am I presumed unable to work` MEANS
    IF `a certificate says I still have COVID-19 on day 21`
    THEN `the later day of` `day 21` `and` `the end of the incapacity the certificate expects`
    ELSE `day 21`
    WHERE
        `day 21` MEANS `the day` 21 `days after` `the date of my injury`

-- cl 5C(3)-(5): a "relevant worker" is one the s 19B(1) presumption covers, for whom the s 19B(5) presumption (unable to
-- work) is rebutted. (4) s 33 applies to such a worker with a total or partial incapacity. (5) "A relevant worker to
-- whom section 33 ... does not otherwise apply is taken to be partially incapacitated for work and to have current work
-- capacity ... during the worker's isolation period if the worker's actual gross weekly earnings from paid employment
-- during that period are -- (a) less than the gross weekly amount that the worker had the capacity to earn in the
-- worker's pre-injury employment immediately before the injury, or (b) nil." (7) the isolation period is the period a
-- doctor requires the worker to isolate after the diagnosis.
@export During my COVID-19 isolation, am I taken to be partially incapacitated for work (Regulation cl 5C(5))?
GIVEN `the COVID-19 presumption covers me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the s 19B(1) presumption applies to you (you contracted COVID-19 while in prescribed employment)
      `the presumption that I could not work was rebutted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the presumption that you were unable to work (s 19B(5)) has been rebutted
      `section 33 applies to me anyway` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you already have a total or partial incapacity for work resulting from the infection, so that s 33 applies to you without clause 5C(5)
      `the week is in my isolation period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the week asked about is within the period a doctor required you to isolate after your diagnosis
      `my actual gross earnings that week` IS A NUMBER @desc Your actual gross weekly earnings from paid employment in that week, in dollars (0 if nil)
      `what I could earn before the injury` IS A NUMBER @desc The gross weekly amount you had the capacity to earn in your pre-injury employment immediately before the injury, in dollars
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I taken to be partially incapacitated during isolation` MEANS
    IF `the COVID-19 presumption covers me` AND `the presumption that I could not work was rebutted`
    THEN IF `section 33 applies to me anyway`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: (5) applies only where s 33 "does not otherwise apply"; (4) says s 33 applies)
         ELSE IF `the week is in my isolation period`
              THEN IF    `my actual gross earnings that week` LESS THAN `what I could earn before the injury`
                      OR `my actual gross earnings that week` EQUALS 0
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE
              ELSE JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (scope limit with no "only": clause 5C(5) is about relevant workers only)
